+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` now supports `fmt="markdown"`. It uses the project's vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`, then adds a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- I didn't touch `vendor/tabulate` or any tests.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` ran 3 tests, all OK. Before the change, 2 of them failed.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` printed the expected table and `**Total stock value:** 461.93`.
+
+## Not verified
+- I only ran it on the sample `inventory.csv`. I didn't test an empty inventory or cells containing `|`, which the table library doesn't escape.
